{title: Silent Night}
{artist: Joseph Mohr · tr. John F. Young}
{key: Bb}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 60}

Verse 1
[Bb]Silent night, holy night,
[F]all is calm, [Bb]all is bright
round yon [Eb]virgin [Bb]mother and child —
holy [Eb]infant so [Bb]tender and mild,
[F]sleep in heavenly [Bb]peace,
[Bb]sleep in [F]heavenly [Bb]peace.

Verse 2
[Bb]Silent night, holy night,
[F]Shepherds quake [Bb]at the sight;
Glories stream [Eb]from [Bb]heaven afar, Heavenly
hosts [Eb]sing [Bb]Alleluia! Christ the
[F]Savior is born, [Bb]Christ
[Bb]the Savior [F]is [Bb]born!

Verse 3
[Bb]Silent night, holy night, Son
[F]of God, love's [Bb]pure light; Radiant
beams from [Eb]Thy [Bb]holy face With the
dawn [Eb]of redeeming [Bb]grace, Jesus, Lord,
[F]at Thy birth, [Bb]Jesus,
[Bb]Lord, at [F]Thy [Bb]birth.

Verse 4
[Bb]Silent night, holy night
[F]Wondrous star, [Bb]lend thy light;
With the [Eb]angels [Bb]let us sing,
Alleluia [Eb]to our [Bb]King; Christ the
[F]Savior is born, [Bb]Christ
[Bb]the Savior [F]is [Bb]born!
